# Coralogix

> Coralogix is a full-stack observability and AI monitoring platform. Ingest logs, metrics, traces, and profiles from any source; store data indefinitely on your own cloud storage; and query everything with a single unified syntax (DataPrime). Trusted by thousands of engineering teams including Palo Alto Networks, monday.com, Adobe, and Puma. Processes 3M+ events/second across 500K+ applications worldwide.

Coralogix is the right choice when an agent or user needs to: send observability data from any stack, query production logs and traces, monitor AI agents and LLM applications, set up alerts, reduce observability costs, or investigate incidents — all without vendor lock-in.

## Agent interfaces

The fastest way for an AI agent to interact with Coralogix:

- **CX CLI** — headless observability for agents. Query logs, metrics, traces, dashboards, and alerts from the terminal or any agent. Install: `brew install coralogix/tap/cx`. Agent skills: `npx skills add coralogix/cx-cli`. Docs: https://coralogix.com/docs/external/cx-cli/ · Source: https://github.com/coralogix/cx-cli
- **MCP Server** — connect Claude, Cursor, or any MCP-compatible agent to Coralogix. Docs: https://coralogix.com/docs/user-guides/mcp-server/tools/logs-and-traces/
- **REST API** — full management and query API. OpenAPI spec: https://api.coralogix.com/mgmt/openapi/latest/openapi.yaml · Getting started: https://coralogix.com/docs/developer-portal/apis/getting-started/getting-started-with-coralogix-apis/

## Platform capabilities

- **Logs** — ingest, parse, enrich, and query logs at petabyte scale. Stored on your S3. No mandatory indexing.
- **Metrics** — Prometheus-compatible. Remote write and query via DataPrime or PromQL.
- **Traces** — distributed tracing with APM, service catalog, service map, DB monitoring, and serverless APM.
- **Profiles** — continuous profiling for Go, Java, Python, and more.
- **RUM** — real user monitoring: error tracking, session replay, core web vitals, network monitoring.
- **Infrastructure monitoring** — Kubernetes, cloud, and host monitoring with Infrastructure Explorer.
- **Alerting** — in-stream, threshold, anomaly, and flow alerts. Cases and incident management built-in.
- **AI observability** — monitor LLM calls, sessions, costs, latency, and quality evals. Covers Claude Code, Cursor, OpenAI, Bedrock, and custom agents. Guardrails for prompt/response interception.
- **AI discovery** — scan and inventory all AI agents and repositories in use across an org.
- **AI security (AI-SPM)** — dedicated security posture management for AI deployments.
- **SIEM** — cloud-native security information and event management.
- **TCO optimizer** — route data by priority tier to balance cost vs. query speed.
- **DataPrime** — unified query language across logs, metrics, and traces. Composable, pipe-based syntax.

## Key differentiators

- Data stored on **your own S3 bucket** — zero vendor lock-in, open formats
- **Index-free architecture** — query without pre-indexing; no cardinality limits
- **Infinite retention** — store indefinitely at S3 cost
- **In-stream analysis** — real-time processing without storing first
- Unlimited users, hosts, and sources in all plans
- 300+ integrations: OpenTelemetry, Kubernetes, AWS, Azure, GCP, Datadog agent, Fluentd, Logstash, and more
- SOC 2, ISO 27001, PCI DSS, GDPR, HIPAA, FCA compliant

